/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:1:Choice: A — reserve evaluation-only TRAIN dates prospectively, but reject the controller’s claim that this is a small-cost change.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:7:**A is defensible; “dates are abundant” is not its justification.** The strongest reason for A is an explicit, auditable boundary between the environments that shaped the learned policy and those supporting an unseen-date claim. The strongest objection is that the controller has already allocated almost the entire TRAIN archive to evaluation. The superseding design calls for approximately 160 claim dates, two worlds per date, six arms and sixteen learner seeds. With only 166 TRAIN dates, preserving 160 evaluation dates leaves at most six training dates before development exclusions or another embargo. A therefore requires a substantive panel and power amendment. It cannot be presented as completing a minor missing allocation detail. See [contract v1, D1](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:28) and [amendment v1.1, item 1](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:14).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:100:5. [Pilot declaration](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:13): **“Stage 4g → its audit → seal package → a-r0 matrix → admission trichotomy → PHYSICS-GO → confirmatory source generation and training on the claim panel with 16 seeds.”** “Training on the claim panel” directly conflicts with evaluation-only A. An amendment must resolve this, rather than treating A as unambiguously implied by existing prose.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-datepool-ws/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:102:6. [Stage 8 v1](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:28): **“D1. Panel: 6 arms × 12 learner seeds × 2 worlds per TRAIN date over the ≈ 160 claim dates (≈ 320 worlds per arm-seed; ≈ 30 steps per world), allocation manifest sealed with role-wise date disjointness (claim dates unused by any successor development activity; legacy overlap recorded); no TEST.”** The seed count was later amended to sixteen. The date commitment cannot be carried into A unchanged while assuming plentiful source dates; the role-wise assertion does not certify source separation.
