/home/sat/mcrl-v025-dates-ws/DATE-ALLOCATION-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:87:**Verified.** V1.1 changes the design to 16 learner seeds, two worlds per date and approximately 160 claim dates. It explicitly **withdraws and replaces** v1 §E's analytic power statement with the measured synthetic calibration table: at 16 seeds, conjunction success 0.675 ± 0.065 at 5% date SD, and 0.980 ± 0.019 at 3% date SD, with seed SD 1% and planning alternative +2% against the +0.5% margin. It discloses nominal-95% interval undercoverage. V1.2 preserves the panel and margins and additionally requires calibration of the decision bound's own one-sided coverage. That is the governing statement before this allocation amendment, not the original “+1% is undetectable” paragraph. [H/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:3–17; H/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:3,8.]
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-dates-ws/DATE-ALLOCATION-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:128:The one completed learner date and the 30 opened diagnostic dates contribute **zero completed fresh claim dates**. Unopened reservations establish assignment, not completed claim evaluation. Tape existence also cannot be inferred from the ceiling receipts: their tapes were held in RAM and not serialised. [W/DATE-VARIANCE-2026-09-09.md:69–80; A/CEILING30-CODEX-2026-09-10.md:82.]
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-dates-ws/DATE-ALLOCATION-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:136:**Answer and final ruling.** I accept those limitations and reject the claim that a 160-date calibration already certifies this experiment. I nevertheless choose **116 source/development, 48 evaluation-only, two quarantined**, because it fixes the missing operational boundary, preserves broad training support and clean start-date evaluation, and is compatible with measured date-only precision at the pre-existing +2% planning alternative without consuming TEST or choosing favourable outcomes. The panel estimates performance on these source-excluded historical TRAIN starts; it is not asserted to be a probability sample of all 166 dates. Actual claim power and residual date dependence must be reported honestly, and failure remains an admissible outcome. The allocation is final; uncertainty about efficacy is not authority to change its dates, margins, model or sign rules after results.
