/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/PROVISIONING-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:39:The v1.8 amendment makes the numerator and setpoint semantics explicit:
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/PROVISIONING-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:41:> “**Traffic model declared explicitly.** The numerator is saturated (full-buffer) decodable throughput under a per-user rate-target power controller; the rate target is a **power-control setpoint, not a demand model**, and realised per-user rates may exceed it. Reported alongside every claim: rate attainment, availability and the coverage/outage distribution. Finite demand or queues would be a versioned model amendment with affected comparisons re-run, never a relabelling.”
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/PROVISIONING-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:43:Source: [v1.8 amendment, §5](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.8-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:9).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/PROVISIONING-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:49:It also required the engine to report “`m_target`, `m_tx` and the realised outcome separately per user-step.” Source: [v1.8 amendment, §8](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.8-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:12). The text therefore expressly distinguishes the rate-target mode from the transmitted mode.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/PROVISIONING-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:87:Consequently the target mode cannot qualify in that view: the transmitted mode is a lower mode if one clears, otherwise no mode is transmitted. A lower mode can decode while its spectral efficiency remains below the `r*n/W` needed for the nominal per-user target. This is exactly the distinction between `m_target`, `m_tx`, decoded PHY service, and separately reported rate attainment that v1.1 and v1.8 require.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/PROVISIONING-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:95:Because this decision makes no model change, v1.8 §5's rerun requirement is not triggered. If a later decision chooses target-mode delivery at the design percentile as a new planning objective, that would reverse v1.9 §1 and would require a versioned amendment and reruns of every affected comparison. That hypothetical is not part of this closed item.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/PROVISIONING-DECISION-2026-09-10.md:103:This reading survives the anti-straw-man check. It accepts the opposing side's strongest evidence—the zero attainments, the 846,846 insufficient-SE decodes, STRICT's restored attainment, the rank-order change, and v1.8's reserve language—and answers the actual contractual question. It does not replace that question with the weaker claim that the alternative is mathematically invalid or inconsequential. The alternative is coherent and consequential; it is simply a policy change, not a correction compelled by breach.
